
# The product changelog is APPEND-ONLY and its order is computed at runtime
# (src/lib/changelog.ts sorts by version), so two branches that each add a
# release entry have no reason to conflict — union keeps both sides' added
# lines and the sort puts them right.
#
# Without this, every release inserts at the same first line, so a branch that
# sits while several releases land collides with all of them. That happened on
# 2026-09-15: seven releases in a day left auto/COSMOS-158 unrebaseable and its
# change had to be lifted onto a fresh branch by hand.
#
# Safe for ADDING entries; if two branches rewrite the SAME entry, union keeps
# both texts and a human has to pick.
src/lib/changelog.ts merge=union
